# Update Roadmap Rule

## Purpose

Govern how [docs/ROADMAP.md](docs/ROADMAP.md) is updated and maintained. Ensures consistency between product roadmap, epics, features, user stories, and implementation plans.

## When to Update ROADMAP

- **New epic or feature**: Add to ROADMAP before or during implementation
- **Completed milestone**: Mark as done, add completion date
- **Scope change**: Update pillars, sections, or tables when product direction changes
- **Plan alignment**: Sync `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md` with ROADMAP epics/features

## Format

### Structure

- **Product Pillars**: High-level categories (Data Labeling, Annotation, Evaluation, Customer-Facing Export)
- **Sections**: Numbered (1. Database Portfolio, 2. Deliverable Pipeline, etc.)
- **Tables**: Use markdown tables for databases, commands, deliverables
- **Epics**: Group related features; use `## Epic N: Title` when adding new work
- **Features**: Sub-items under epics; use `### N.M Feature Name`
- **User Stories**: Format `US-N.M`: As a [role], I want [action] so that [benefit]

### Versioning

- Add `Last Updated: YYYY-MM-DD` at bottom when making substantive changes
- Link plan files: `See .cursor/plans/roadmap_*.plan.md for implementation details`

## Linking to Epics and Plans

- Each epic in ROADMAP should have a corresponding plan or todo list
- Reference plan files: `[.cursor/plans/roadmap_rules_skills_and_features_*.plan.md](.cursor/plans/)`
- User stories (US-N.M) map to implementation todos

## Integration

- **qa-workflow-cursor.mdc**: References this rule for roadmap maintenance
- **Product management skill**: Use when creating epics, features, user stories, todos
